  "slug": "estaba-estuve-gerundio",
  "titulo": "Imperfect progressive vs preterite progressive (was + -ing)",
  "subtitulo": "Estaba lloviendo / Estuvimos bailando toda la noche.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Estaba + gerund describes what was going on, often interrupted by another action. Estuve + gerund is an ongoing action inside a closed time frame: estuvimos bailando toda la noche, de 6 a 7.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English has one _was + -ing_. Spanish has two, depending on the time frame."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "estaba + gerund (imperfect progressive)",
              "describes what was going on; no start or end in view; often interrupted",
              "Estaba cocinando cuando llamaste."
            ],
            [
              "estuve + gerund (preterite progressive)",
              "an ongoing action inside a closed, finished time frame",
              "Estuve cocinando toda la tarde."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The preterite progressive usually comes with a time phrase that closes the action: **toda la noche, de 6 a 7, el sábado pasado, dos horas, hasta que...**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **estaba** is a movie still; **estuve** is the whole clip, start to end."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "estaba",
      "titulo": "Estaba + gerund",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Susana ==estaba escribiendo== una carta.",
              "en": "Susana was writing a letter."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los niños ==estaban jugando== en el jardín.",
              "en": "The kids were playing in the yard."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Qué ==estaban haciendo==? —==Estábamos viendo== la tele.",
              "en": "—What were you doing? —We were watching TV."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ella ==se estaba lavando== el pelo cuando él llegó.",
              "en": "She was washing her hair when he arrived."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For describing a scene, it's often interchangeable with the plain imperfect: **Estaba lloviendo y la gente estaba corriendo** = **Llovía y la gente corría**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "estuve",
      "titulo": "Estuve + gerund",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==estuvimos bailando== toda la noche.",
              "en": "Yesterday we were dancing all night."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué ==estuvieron haciendo== de seis a siete?",
              "en": "What were you doing from six to seven?"
            },
            {
              "es": "El sábado pasado ==estuve calificando== exámenes.",
              "en": "Last Saturday I was grading exams."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Estuvimos comiendo== hasta que se acabó todo y luego nos fuimos al cine.",
              "en": "We were eating until everything was gone, and then we went to the movies."
